                 to be set.  At least one such string OID=[syntax:]value
                 should be provided to bbssnnmmppsseett to be able to send a request.

                 OOIIDD
                   OID may be input as a string, a string followed by a random
                   number of integers (suboids) separated by dots, a sequence
                   of integers separated by dots - that is if the _n option is
                   used - and in such case a syntax is required for every
                   value, or a string followed by square brackets (used to de‐
                   note an entry's indexes) and corresponding indexes.  Any of
                   the formats used to print a single variable by bbssnnmmppsseett is
                   valid as input OID as well:

                   1.3.6.1.2.1.25.1.1.0=TimeTicks:537615486

                   sysLocation=OctetString:"@ Home" (with --oo _v_e_r_b_o_s_e option)

                   sysLocation.0="@ Home"

